# URLs the links workflow does not check, each with the reason it cannot
# be checked. A host that is only slow or throttles is answered by the
# retries and the --accept of btclib-org/.github's reusable-links.yml
# instead. lychee reads this file from the directory it runs in, the
# checkout root, and takes each line that is neither empty nor a comment
# as a regular expression.

# git.rust-bitcoin.org answers lychee with a 403 page asking it to prove
# it is human, on GitHub's runners and on a desktop alike, so lychee
# cannot check a link to it (issues #689 and #704). COMPARISON.md cites
# corepc pull request 739 there, which github.com/rust-bitcoin/corepc,
# the repository corepc moved from, does not carry.
^https://git\.rust-bitcoin\.org/
